<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahipala I (Pala)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 988–1038</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-i-gurjara-pratihara">Mahipala I</a> was king of the Pala dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> from about 988 to 1038. He revived Pala power after a century of decline by recovering northern and eastern Bengal, and he restored Buddhist monasteries. His reign saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> expedition of Rajendra I to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> around 1021–1023, which claimed a victory over him.</p></div>
